        "timestamp": 1794914475,
        "reasoning": "Confirmed the stale-reply hypothesis path: on error (`m.finish(a, StatusError, ...)`) the target appends a **user** message but no assistant message. So `lastAssistantText(target)` returns whatever the previous assistant message was — stale. And ask_agent returns `tool.OK`.\n\nNow, how to trigger error with mock backend? Provider \"mock\" — client.Stream error? Maybe mock always succeeds. I can simulate the target failing by setting `a.Backend = \"loop\"` with provider mock → executeLoop immediately calls `m.finish(a, StatusError, \"loop backend 需要真实模型...\")`. That's a clean, deterministic way to make the target produce no assistant text!\n\nSo test:\n1. m := NewManager(mock)\n2. a := Create(\"a\",\"甲\"), b := Create(\"b\",\"乙\")\n3. b.Messages preloaded with {assistant, \"旧答案：42\"} — directly set (test is in same package)\n4. b.Backend = \"loop\"  → 执行即报 StatusError「loop backend 需要真实模型」\n5. run askAgentTool from a to 乙\n6. Expected (correct): Status != OK, because this round produced no reply.\n   Actual (buggy): Status == OK and content contains \"旧答案：42\" → proves stale-reply bug.\n\nWait — does `executeLoop` need cfg.Provider == \"mock\"? Yes: `if cfg.Provider == \"mock\" || cfg.Provider == \"\"` → finish error. Good, with mock provider it errors immediately. \n\nLet me write this test as a real file to run it. Where? Add to internal/agent/ask_tool_test.go? Better: create a temporary probe test file `internal/agent/ask_stale_probe_test.go`, run it, and then decide whether to keep (it's a legit regression test). I'll name it properly and keep it if it demonstrates a real bug. But careful: I shouldn't commit a test asserting buggy behavior. I'll write it as a test that asserts the *correct* behavior (fails now, showing the bug), then report to the agent.\n\nLet me write and run.\n\nAlso worth testing: cycle protection across 3 hops (A→B→C→A). beginAsk walks chain via waiting map — it should catch. The existing test only covers 2 nodes. Let me