nd-to-end that mirrors production, I could use a fake HTTP server as an OpenAI-compatible endpoint. That's heavy. \n\nAlternative approach: test the *communication* path end-to-end using create_agent without task (creation), then manually set child backend to \"mock\", then ask_agent from parent → verify reply round-trips, both histories updated, and reply content correct. That covers \"创建子agent 进行协助 + 通信正常\" realistically, plus the create-with-task path is covered by existing tests (returns graceful failure).\n\nAdditionally test: parallel fan-out — parent creates 2 helpers, asks both concurrently from two goroutines; verify both replies received and no deadlock/race. Run with -race to check concurrency safety (my role: 并发安全). That's valuable: `go test -race`.\n\nLet me write this test file: `internal/agent/subagent_comm_test.go` with:\n- TestSubAgentCreateThenCommunicate: create 帮手 via createAgentTool, verify appears in list_agents, set backend mock, ask_agent from parent, verify OK + content contains marker, verify child Messages has the task and an assistant reply, verify parent's history unaffected (parent didn't pollute own messages).\n- TestSubAgentParallelFanOut: 1 parent + 3 helpers, ask all concurrently, with -race, verify all OK and each reply distinct (to catch cross-talk: each helper replies with its own name).\n- TestCreateThenAskSameNameRace? maybe skip.\n\nAlso worth testing: `list_agents` excludes nothing (it lists all including self) — the tool description says \"看现在有哪些会话\". Fine.\n\nPotential real bug to probe: **`createAgentTool` + `askAgentTool` share `beginAsk` cycle guard keyed by fromID. create+ask uses the SAME fromID as parent → if parent already has an outstanding ask... nested. E.g., A asks B; B creates C and asks C: beginAsk(A)=B, then beginAsk(B)=C → fine. Then C asks A → blocked. Good.\n\nAnother potential bug: **create_agent doesn't inherit Backend** → in production with claude backend parent, child gets \"loop\" + real provider config → works. OK.\n\nAnother potential bug: **maxAgents** — check it exists. grep maxAgents.\n\nLet me also check `Timeout()` on tool — my ask_tool has no Timeout() → default? Check tool.go interface for Timeout and registry default. Earlier loop.go had `context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 5*time.Second)` at line 372 — that might be a default per-tool timeout, which would mean `ask_agent` gets killed after 5s! That's a big deal: ask_agent waiting for a real LLM reply takes longer than 5s. Let me check loop.go:372 context.\n\nThat's an important finding for \"通信是否正常\". Let me look."
